  "worked_solution": "A geometric random variable $X$ with probability of success $p$ has the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=(1-p)^{x-1}p\n$$\n\nLet $X$ be the number of sentences checked until a new typo is found. Since the chance of finding a typo in any sentence is $5%,$ the number of sentences checked until the first typo can be modeled as a geometric random variable with a probability of success\n\n$$\np=5%=\\frac{5}{100}=0.05.\n$$\n\nSo, $X\u223c\\text{Geom}(0.05).$ In this case, $X$ has the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =(1-0.05)^{x-1}(0.05) \\\\  & =(0.95)^{x-1}(0.05)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe require $P(X\\ge 4).$ \n\nTo compute $P(X\\ge 4),$ we will use the complement:\n\n$$\nP(X\\ge 4)=1-P(X<4)\n$$\n\nComputing the probability of the complement, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X<4) & =P(X\\in {1,2,3}) \\\\  & =f(1)+f(2)+f(3) \\\\  & =(0.95)^{1-1}(0.05)+(0.95)^{2-1}(0.05)+(0.95)^{3-1}(0.05) \\\\  & =(0.05)+(0.95)(0.05)+(0.95)^{2}(0.05) \\\\  & =[1+0.95+(0.95)^{2}](0.05) \\\\  & \u22480.143,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places.\n\nTherefore, there are no typos within the first three sentences is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\ge 4) & =1-P(X<4) \\\\  & \u22481-0.143 \\\\  & \u22480.857\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places.",
